<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Royalty payment catapults ICH half yr share.</title>
<headline>Royalty payment catapults ICH half yr share.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     128	  vs    27.87</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 120	  vs    27.00</p>
<p>    Attrib income	    17.70     vs     3.86</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		    30.25     vs     3.86</p>
<p>    Tax			  12.54     vs     --</p>
<p>    Interest received	 1.47     vs     0.79</p>
<p>    Royalty received	 28.89	vs    --</p>
<p>Div payable: April 15</p>
<p>On register: April 4</p>
<p>Full name: Industrial &amp; Commercial Holdings Group Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company owns a 12.5 percent interest in the Saturn Partnership, which entitles ICH to receive royalty income from the Venetia Diamond Mine in the Northern Province.</p>
<p>The company said it received a 28.89 million rand royalty in the six months to December, while a further 22.94 million rand royalty was received on February 28 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
